## Lane Detection

| User intent | Lane |
|-------------|------|
| Ask, tell, talk, consult, research, explain, how-to, brainstorm, decide, clarify | Advisory → `/sc-discuss` when mission-scoped |
| Add, build, create, implement, develop, feature, make | Mission → `/sc-run` after discuss clear |
| Fix, debug, diagnose, broken, error, bug, crash, investigate | Debug |
| Edit prompt, config, doc, small fix, human already made changes, just commit | Quick |

## Cursor Mode Bridge

| User intent | Lane | Cursor mode / action |
|---|---|---|
| Ask / explain / clarify / visual draft | Discuss | Agent + `/sc-discuss` |
| Roadmap implement | Mission | Agent + `/sc-run` (after discuss clear) |
| Bug hunt | Debug | Cursor Debug Mode |
| Ship | Ship | Agent + `/sc-ship` |
| Small edit / commit | Quick | Agent + `/sc-quick` (no mission; still INTENT/AUTH/TWINS/3-cycle) |

After `/sc-discuss` clears clarify (and visual draft when required), prefer new session `/sc-run`; no non-blocking questions mid-AFK. Mission ship only via `/sc-ship`; no-mission small edits via `/sc-quick`. Detail: `.cursor/skills/sc-discuss`, `sc-run`, `sc-ship`, `sc-quick`, `sc-mission`.

## Lifecycle (canonical)

```
/sc-discuss (HIL clear) → new session /sc-run (build → drain → ready) → human check → /sc-ship
```

- **Discuss:** spec, decisions, visual draft HIL, mission brief (Accept/Adjust/Reject) → `clarify-status clear`. Handoff: `Spec clear. New session: /sc-run.`
- **Run:** plan → build → combine(+UI) → issues drain → review + `sc-judge` → `ready`. Handoff: `Ready. Human check, then /sc-ship.`
- **Ship:** squash checkpoints ≤5, closeout, merge `--no-ff`, archive. Roadmap continues: `Next: new session → /sc-discuss <id>`

Detail: `/sc-discuss`, `/sc-run`, `/sc-ship`. Issues policy: **sc-learn**; drain loop owned by **sc-run**. Local trust (gitignored): `.space/trust/lessons.md` - read before discuss/plan/run; seed from sc-learn `references/trust-seed/` if missing.

`spacecraft map use|current|next` select and advance the roadmap.

## Roadmap / issues

- ≤7 jigsaw tasks per phase as a hard Must (not preference-only). Reject soft prefer ≤7; reject any 8-9 exception band.
- Escape hatches when scope exceeds ≤7 (not a higher or soft cap):
  - Same-mission phase split: sequential `plan-phaseN.json` (or `plan-phase1.json`, …) under the mission.
  - Roadmap / multi-mission: `spacecraft map new`, then add missions; discuss each, AFK with `/sc-run`.
- Issues: record in mission `issues.md`; drain in `/sc-run` until 0 open (policy in sc-learn). Ready/ship: 0 open issues, 0 review findings. Fix issue #N: view → mission → spec → close after ship.

## Mission resolution

Branch `feat/<id>/…` → `.space/missions/<id>/mission.json`. List: `ls .space/missions/`. State: `spacecraft set-state [id] <state>` (`state` alias). CLI: `evidence`/`evi`, `validate`/`val`, `roadmap`/`map`.

Clarify status: `open` | `clear` | `deferred` under mission dir.

## Lanes (pointers)

- **Discuss:** `/sc-discuss` (spec, decisions, visual draft, mission brief before clear). Detail: `sc-clarify`, `sc-ux-design` (brief/draft), `sc-discuss/references/mission-brief.md`.
- **Mission:** `/sc-run` (plan → build → drain → review → ready). Detail: `sc-mission`, `sc-planning`, `sc-tdd`, `sc-verification`, `sc-learn`, `sc-judge` (block on `REFUTED`). Shares INTENT / AUTH / TWINS / 3-cycle with Quick.
- **Ship:** `/sc-ship` - validate, rebase, merge `--no-ff`, archive (mission only).
- **Quick:** `/sc-quick` - no mission artifacts; branch `<type>/<title>` → verify → commit → ship with `SPACECRAFT_SHIP=1 SPACECRAFT_QUICK=1` (hook skips closeout). Still git safety + tests; **does not skip** INTENT / AUTH / TWINS / 3-cycle. Do not invent a mission stub.
- **Debug:** reproduce E2E → falsify root cause → record in `issues.md`. Prefer Cursor Debug Mode for runtime evidence.

## Subagent Delegation

Orchestrator, not implementer. Task-delegate:

| Agent | Role |
|---|---|
| `sc-coder` | production code |
| `sc-tester` | tests + evidence |
| `sc-planner` | plan.json |
| `sc-reviewer` | release readiness (requires `sc-judge` before ready) |
| `sc-designer` | UI critique (required before discuss draft HIL; also run review) |
| `sc-adviser` | complex design (discuss) |
| `sc-firmware` | STM32 C |

Patterns: visual draft approved in `/sc-discuss` before `/sc-run`; tester before coder (one acceptance per pair); firmware for embedded; combine then issues drain; UI visual + functional recheck in run; reviewer + `sc-judge` before ready (block on `REFUTED`); reviewer before ship.

## Inner-loop gates

Always-on for **Quick and Mission** alike (see also `000-spacecraft`). Quick skips mission ceremony (spec/plan/TDD/formal review) but not these gates:

- **INTENT:** Before behavior-changing edits (code / check / spec), emit `INTENT:` with class + intended behavior. Authority when disagreement: explicit user > spec > tests > current code. "Make tests pass" alone is not intended behavior.
- **AUTH:** Before push / deploy / publish / send, emit `AUTH:` with a quoted user authorization. Necessary but not sufficient for ship - `/sc-ship` or `/sc-quick`, hooks, and `SPACECRAFT_SHIP=1` still apply (`SPACECRAFT_QUICK=1` for quick). AUTH does not bypass those gates; merge/push/tag still require `SPACECRAFT_SHIP=1`.
- **TWINS:** After defect fixes, emit `TWINS:` with project-wide search for the same construct / twin occurrences before claiming done. After **3 failed fix-verify cycles**, stop and hand back to human (no more looping).

## Session Handoff

Unfinished work: state, blockers, dirty git, next pickup. Prefer new session when phase changes (discuss → run → ship). End with recommended next action.
